cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or experimental baseline, please cite the accompanying working paper."
title: "Commitment-Based Knowledge Distillation: Statistical Certification and Optimistic Verification for Trust-Minimized Model Serving"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rufino
    given-names: Antonio
version: "Baseline V1"
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Antoniorjr4/commitment-based-knowledge-distillation"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for component-level experiments on statistical
  certification and optimistic verification for commitment-based knowledge
  distillation. The repository preserves the frozen Baseline V1 EVM arbiter,
  test harness, benchmark protocol, reported results, and automated reproduction
  workflow. The components are research prototypes and are not an integrated
  production system.
